<script>import {LABELS} from '@lib/ai/labels';import {ShieldCheck,Cpu,ArrowUpRight} from 'lucide-svelte';</script>
<div class="page-title"><div><h1>Model & privacy guide</h1><p>Understand what happens behind every frame.</p></div><a class="btn outline" href="/detect/image">Try detection <ArrowUpRight size={15}/></a></div><article class="guide"><section><Cpu size={25}/><h2>Built to run where you are.</h2><p>Visionary AI uses Ultralytics YOLOv8n-seg, trained on the COCO dataset. ONNX Runtime Web runs the model in a dedicated browser worker, preferring WebGPU and falling back to WebAssembly. The input is a letterboxed 640 × 640 RGB image.</p><p>The model predicts 80 categories, boxes, and instance segmentation masks. Objects outside these categories may not be recognized. Confidence is a model score, not a calibrated probability of correctness.</p><p>Live counts describe the latest analyzed frame. Visionary AI does not track identities or count unique objects across time. Analyzed frames are shown with matching overlays to keep shapes aligned.</p><p>Latency varies with hardware and browser. Camera access needs HTTPS or localhost. Mobile browsers may use the slower WebAssembly fallback.</p></section><section><ShieldCheck size={25}/><h2>Your data, frame by frame.</h2><p>Live camera frames and uploaded images stay in your browser during analysis. Model files and runtime binaries are downloaded from the configured host and jsDelivr. No external AI prediction API is used.</p><p>Clicking Save sends one compressed snapshot to authenticated Cloudinary storage and its detection metadata to your account in PostgreSQL. Only authorized requests obtain temporary signed image access. Links remain usable until their short expiry, so keep them private.</p><p>Deleting a snapshot removes it from your account immediately. A durable cleanup queue retries image deletion if storage is temporarily unavailable. Unsaved uploads are reconciled by the scheduled cleanup job.</p><p>Your password is hashed with Argon2id. Sessions use short-lived JWTs, rotating refresh cookies, server-side revocation, and CSRF protection. Predictions submitted by the browser are treated as unverified client data.</p></section><section><h2>80 ways to see the everyday.</h2><div class="labels-list">{#each LABELS as label}<span>{label}</span>{/each}</div></section><section><h2>Model provenance & license</h2><p>YOLOv8n-seg weights and the Ultralytics toolchain are distributed under AGPL-3.0, with commercial licensing available from Ultralytics. Model export, evaluation, and validation commands live in the repository’s ml directory.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://docs.ultralytics.com/tasks/segment/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ultralytics segmentation documentation <ArrowUpRight size={15}/></a><a class="text-link" href="https://onnxruntime.ai/docs/tutorials/web/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ONNX Runtime Web documentation <ArrowUpRight size={15}/></a></section></article>
